/-! # Faithful semilinear action on an invariant open and stable Cartier pullback

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, X 2.3 Step 2, printed p.150; Stacks Project,
Tags 01I2, 01HB, 02OO (6) and 01WV.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-semilinear-open-faithful-cartier)

The ambient map is the actual fibre-product map, using the inverse scalar automorphism.
The Cartier ideal is the existing extended inverse-image ideal `IdealSheafData.comap`.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The canonical semilinear map `id_B × Spec(h⁻¹)` on a scalar extension.
The compatibility in `pullback.map` is the image under `Spec` of the algebra
homomorphism's identity on scalars; no map is chosen from an existence assertion.

Source: ILO X 2.3 Step 2, p.150; Stacks 01I2 and the fibre-product universal property.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-semilinear-open-faithful-cartier) -/
noncomputable def semilinearBaseChangeMap
    (e L : Type u) [Field e] [Field L] [Algebra e L]
    {B : Scheme.{u}} (b : B ⟶ Spec (.of e)) (h : L ≃ₐ[e] L) :
    pullback b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))) ⟶
      pullback b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))) :=
  pullback.map b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L)))
    b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L)))
    (𝟙 B) (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom h.symm.toRingHom)) (𝟙 _)
    ((Category.comp_id b).trans (Category.id_comp b).symm)
    ((Category.comp_id _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun f : e →+* L => Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom f))
        h.symm.toAlgHom.comp_algebraMap).symm.trans
          (Spec.map_comp (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))
            (CommRingCat.ofHom h.symm.toRingHom))))

/-- Restriction of the canonical semilinear maps to a nonempty invariant open gives a
faithful left action by scheme automorphisms over the original base. The second projection
is semilinear with the inverse scalar automorphism. Every flatly pulled-back effective
Cartier ideal is Cartier, has inverse-image support, and is fixed as an ideal sheaf.

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, X 2.3 Step 2, printed p.150; Stacks 01I2, 01HB,
02OO (6), and 01WV. (blueprint: lem-sfb-semilinear-open-faithful-cartier)

Proof (the four steps of the DAG):
1. Contravariant functoriality of Spec and the fibre-product universal property give
   alpha_1 = id and alpha_h composed with alpha_k = alpha_(hk): on the scalar projection
   the composite is Spec(k⁻¹ composed with h⁻¹) = Spec((hk)⁻¹). The first projection is
   unchanged. Stability for h and h⁻¹ gives an automorphism of the open. Restricting
   these equations gives the action laws and both projection formulas. Preservation
   of the first projection makes these automorphisms e-morphisms.
2. If a restricted automorphism is identity, choose a point of the nonempty open.
   Its scalar map L to its residue field is injective. Applying the residue-field map
   to the second projection formula gives lambda = lambda composed with h⁻¹, by
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-map-residue-field-naturality. Injectivity gives h = 1. The scalar
   action itself is faithful since H is a subgroup of the algebra automorphism group.
3. Apply lem-pc-flat-pullback-effective-cartier-ideal to the assumed flat restriction
   of the first projection. On an affine chart the pulled-back ideal is generated by
   the image of a regular generator, which remains regular by flatness. This is
   precisely the extended ideal given by IdealSheafData.comap.
4. The inverse-image formula for Spec on prime ideals identifies the support. Since
   the first projection is invariant, a pulled-back local generator stays the same
   after another pullback by r_h. Thus the extended ideals agree on a cover, hence
   globally. The unit generator handles the empty divisor, giving the unit ideal
   and empty support. No finiteness, separability, normality, properness or integrality
   is used in any step.
-/
theorem exists_semilinear_open_faithful_cartier
    (e L : Type u) [Field e] [Field L] [Algebra e L]
    (H : Subgroup (L ≃ₐ[e] L)) (B : Scheme.{u}) (b : B ⟶ Spec (.of e))
    (U : (pullback b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L)))).Opens)
    (hne : Nonempty U.toScheme)
    (hstable : ∀ h : H, U ≤ (semilinearBaseChangeMap e L b h.val) ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    [Flat (U.ι ≫ pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))))] :
    ∃ r : H →* Aut U.toScheme,
      (∀ h : H, (r h).hom ≫ U.ι = U.ι ≫ semilinearBaseChangeMap e L b h.val) ∧
      (∀ h : H, (r h).hom ≫ U.ι ≫
          pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))) =
        U.ι ≫ pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L)))) ∧
      (∀ h : H, (r h).hom ≫ U.ι ≫
          pullback.snd b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))) =
        U.ι ≫ pullback.snd b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))) ≫
          Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom h.val.symm.toRingHom)) ∧
      (∀ h : H, (r h).hom = 𝟙 U.toScheme → h = 1) ∧
      (∀ h : H, (∀ a : L, h.val a = a) → h = 1) ∧
      (∀ I : B.IdealSheafData, I.IsInvertible →
        (I.comap (U.ι ≫
          pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))))).IsInvertible ∧
        ((I.comap (U.ι ≫
          pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))))).support :
            Set U.toScheme) =
          (U.ι ≫ pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L)))) ⁻¹'
            (I.support : Set B) ∧
        ∀ h : H, (I.comap (U.ι ≫
          pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))))).comap
            (r h).hom =
          I.comap (U.ι ≫
            pullback.fst b (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap e L))))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
